            "timestamp": "2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00",
            "curator": "edison_literature_identity",
            "action": "ANNOTATED",
            "changes": "Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/Colloidal_chitin-edison-literature.md (local artifact \u2014 research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather than linked). Report verdict: **Recommended interpretation:** \u201ccolloidal chitin\u201d is not a discrete small chemical, salt, hydrate, buffer, or invariant commercial formulation. It is a **protocol-defined, finely dispersed/pretreated form of the chitin polymer**, usually retained as a hydrated preparation or suspension for culture media and chitinase assays. In the best recovered preparation-level evidence, purified shrimp-derive CURIEs discussed: CHEBI:17029, MESH:D002798. Recorded as provenance only \u2014 no grounding applied from this run. Edison's recommendations are deliberately conservative, and a plausible identifier promoted by a mechanism that never decided anything is what #203 and #263 exist to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator's to accept or reject.",
            "llm_assisted": true
          },
          {
            "timestamp": "2026-11-08T05:26:02.116293+00:00",
            "curator": "codex_worker04_biological",
            "action": "ANNOTATED_SOURCE_BOUND_PROTOCOL",
            "changes": "Proposed annotation of primary DSMZ1681 protocol linked to MediaDive1506. Maintains generic owner UNMAPPED and preserves commercial-powder alternative; no exact chitin mapping or generic whole-owner preparation claim. Primary source: https://bacmedia.dsmz.de/pdf/1681",
            "previous_status": "UNMAPPED",
            "new_status": "UNMAPPED",
            "llm_assisted": true
          }
        ],
        "notes": "Imported from mim-queue (source_id=mediadive.ingredient:1506); no CAS-RN or CHEBI/NCIT match. Reviewed on 2026-05-11 as a prepared chitin substrate form pending exact polymer preparation curation. Source-bound 2026-11-08 review: DSMZ1681, one of the MediaDive1506 recipe uses, specifies commercial crab (shrimp) shell flakes treated with hydrochloric acid, precipitated into cold water, centrifuged and washed to pH6-6.5. The recipe lists 5g colloidal chitin and permits commercial chitin powder as an alternative. This evidence describes that source protocol only; it does not establish that every generic colloidal-chitin source is made by this method, identify a single polymer fraction/acetylation state, or promote the owner to CHEBI:17029. Full primary capture is retained in the worker04 source-review bundle.",
        "ingredient_type": "UNDEFINED_MIXTURE"
      }
    }
